# Line endings.
#
# This repo is developed on Windows and deployed on Linux. git's autocrlf
# normalises to LF in the object store and hands Windows CRLF on checkout,
# which is fine for source — but NOT for files Linux executes or parses by
# line. A shell script checked out with CRLF fails as
#     /usr/bin/env: 'bash\r': No such file or directory
# and a systemd unit with CRLF silently mis-parses its directives.
#
# So: normalise text, and pin LF on everything that runs on the server.

* text=auto

*.sh            text eol=lf
*.service       text eol=lf
*.conf          text eol=lf
*.conf.example  text eol=lf
.env.example    text eol=lf

# Binary — never touch these.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.mp3  binary
*.mp4  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.xlsx binary
